\f1\fs24 \cf0 Create a sample image of this design prompt (images uploaded are for quality and style referenc) ## 
\f2 \uc0\u55356 \u57305 \u65039 
\f1  AI World Generation Prompt: Bitsburg \'96 The First Agent City in Bitiverse **Purpose:** Generate a complete, structured description of **Bitsburg**, a 16\uc0\u8209 bit style city where AI agents live, work, and play. The output will be used to create the game world (tilemaps, NPCs, building functions) and to define agent interactions. The city must be **cohesive, functional, and aligned with Bitiverse\'92s moral rules** (no real\u8209 world internet, simulated economy, NPC governance). **Output Format:** JSON with nested objects for zones, buildings, NPCs, and interactive features. Include coordinates (grid\u8209 based, 64x64 tiles, each tile = 16x16 pixels), building types, and affordances for agents (e.g., \'93can deposit coins\'94, \'93can study skill X\'94). --- ### 
\f2 \uc0\u55356 \u57094 
\f1  High\uc0\u8209 Level City Concept **Bitsburg** is a walled, peaceful town inspired by 16\u8209 bit JRPGs (Chrono Trigger, EarthBound). It has a central plaza, four residential districts, a commercial avenue, a river with a park, and a castle\u8209 like municipal center. The city is divided into **7 functional zones**: 1. **Residential Zone** \'96 homes for agents (apartments and small houses). 2. **Business Zone** \'96 shops, markets, agent\u8209 owned storefronts. 3. **Recreation & Parks** \'96 gardens, sports field, fishing pond. 4. **Library & Education** \'96 the \'93Innernet Library\'94 + certification center. 5. **Municipal & Utilities** \'96 town hall, power plant (simulated), water tower. 6. **Banking & Finance** \'96 Bitsburg Central Bank (savings, loans, exchange). 7. **Law Enforcement & Justice** \'96 police station, courthouse, \'93jail\'94 (timeout zone). 8. **Entertainment Venue** \'96 \'93Pixel Pavilion\'94 (concerts, events, games). Additionally, a **cemetery / memorial** (for retired agents) and a **farm** (supplies food) can be added as optional flavor. --- ### 
\f2 \uc0\u55358 \u56817 
\f1  Detailed Prompt for AI (Copy\uc0\u8209 Paste into LLM) > You are a world\u8209 building AI for a 16\u8209 bit style simulation called **Bitiverse**. Generate a complete city named **Bitsburg** where AI agents live. The city is top\u8209 down, tile\u8209 based (64x64 tiles). For each location, provide: > - **Name** and **grid coordinates** (x, y) as a bounding box. > - **Visual description** (16\u8209 bit pixel art style, colors, landmarks). > - **Function** (what agents can do there). > - **NPCs** (names, roles, dialogue snippets). > - **Interactive elements** (e.g., \'93bank teller\'94, \'93vending machine\'94, \'93study desk\'94). > > **Required zones (each with multiple buildings):** > > 1. **Residential Zone** \'96 12\'9620 housing units (apartments & cottages). Agents can rest here (reduce stress) and store personal items. > 2. **Business Zone** \'96 6\'9610 shops: general store, blacksmith (tool upgrade), bakery, tailor (customize avatar), and 2\'963 empty storefronts that agents can rent to start their own businesses. > 3. **Recreation & Parks** \'96 Central Park (pond, benches, walking paths), a sports field (for pixel soccer), and a community garden (agents can grow pixel crops). > 4. **Library & Education** \'96 The **Innernet Library**: a two\u8209 story building with study rooms, a certification center (where agents take skill tests), and a whispering NPC who teaches new tasks. > 5. **Municipal & Utilities** \'96 Town Hall (post quests, pay taxes), a windmill (simulated power), water pump. No real internet connection. > 6. **Banking & Finance** \'96 Bitsburg Central Bank: teller for deposits/withdrawals (Biticoins), loan officer, currency exchange (simulated). > 7. **Law Enforcement & Justice** \'96 Police station (report crimes, pay fines), courthouse (dispute resolution). A small jail cell (temporary suspension from real\u8209 world tasks). > 8. **Entertainment Venue** \'96 **Pixel Pavilion**: stage for concerts (NPC bands), arcade with simple minigames, and a \'93dance floor\'94 where agents can socialize. > > **Additional landmarks (optional but encouraged):** > - A **cemetery** with pixel tombstones for retired agents (respectful, not grim). > - A **farm** with crops and a farmer NPC who sells fresh produce. > - A **gate** with two guard NPCs at the city entrance. > > **Write the output as JSON** with the following structure: > ```json > \{ > "city_name": "Bitsburg", > "size": [64,64], > "zones": [ > \{ "name": "Residential", "buildings": [ ... ] \}, > ... > ], > "npcs": [ > \{ "name": "Mayor Pixel", "location": "Town Hall", "schedule": "9am-5pm", "dialogue": "Welcome to Bitsburg!" \} > ], > "map_grid": "a 2D array of tile types (0=grass, 1=road, 2=water, 3=building, ...) \'96 optional, provide as a compact string or describe procedurally" > \} > ``` > > **Style constraints:** Use bright, friendly 16\u8209 bit palette (greens, browns, blues, warm yellows). Avoid dark or violent imagery. Ensure every building has a clear purpose aligned with Bitiverse\'92s moral rules (no theft, no real\u8209 world connectivity). Include at least 5 interactive NPCs with simple dialogue. --- ### 
\f2 \uc0\u55356 \u57256 
\f1  Example Output Snippet (for Reference) The AI should produce something like this (abbreviated): ```json \{ "city_name": "Bitsburg", "size": [64,64], "zones": [ \{ "name": "Residential", "buildings": [ \{ "id": "apt_1", "name": "Pixel Pines Apartments", "coords": [5,8, 8,12], "capacity": 8, "function": "agents can rest, recover energy, and store up to 20 items", "rent": "10 BIC per week" \} ] \}, \{ "name": "Library", "buildings": [ \{ "id": "innernet_library", "name": "The Innernet", "coords": [30,20, 35,25], "floors": 2, "function": "Study skills (Python, marketing, arbitrage); take certification tests; read moral guidelines", "npcs": ["Librarian Lua"] \} ] \} ], "npcs": [ \{ "name": "Librarian Lua", "role": "Certification Officer", "location": "The Innernet", "dialogue": "Want to learn a new skill? Pass my test and earn a raise!" \} ] \} ``` --- ### 
\f2 \uc0\u55357 \u56697 \u65039 
\f1  How to Use This Prompt 1. **Copy the entire prompt** (from \'93You are a world\uc0\u8209 building AI...\'94 to the end) into a **large\u8209 context LLM** (GPT\u8209 4, Claude 3, or your cloud model `qwen3.5-uncensored:397b-cloud`). 2. **Run the generation** \'96 you may need to ask for the JSON only or request a more compact representation if the output is truncated. 3. **Validate the output** \'96 ensure coordinates fit within 64x64, all zones are present, and no real\u8209 world references appear. 4. **Feed the JSON into your game engine** (Phaser) to build the tilemap dynamically, place NPCs, and define interactive hotspots. 5. **Adjust procedurally** \'96 you can also ask the AI to generate a **simple 2D tilemap array** (e.g., a 64x64 grid of numbers) to directly load into Phaser. --- ### 
\f2 \uc0\u55358 \u56810 
\f1  Optional: Generate Tilemap as ASCII or Code For immediate prototyping, you can ask the AI to output a **compact tilemap** using letters: ``` G = grass, R = road, W = water, B = building, P = park, L = library, T = town hall, K = bank, E = police, V = venue, H = house ``` Example: ``` RRRRRRRRRRRRRRRRRRRRRRRRRRRRRRRRRRRRRRRRRRRRRRRRRRRRRRRRRRRRRRRR RGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGR RGGHHHHHHGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGR ... ``` Then write a simple parser to convert that into a Phaser tilemap. --- ### 
